{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for the Sudoku puzzle are explained, with a notable exception to the standard rules. In this version, the numbers within the cells contained by grey lines must add up to the figures shown in the corner. This variation adds a new level of complexity to the traditional puzzle. The standard rule of not repeating numbers within each shape still applies, ensuring the puzzle remains challenging yet solvable.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the traditional Sudoku rules requires careful attention to the numbers within the grey-lined cells. These numbers must sum up to the values indicated in the corners, a detail that sets this puzzle apart. The constraint of not repeating any number within each shape formed by the grey lines remains, combining with the new rule to create a unique puzzle-solving experience. The interplay between these rules demands a strategic approach, making the puzzle more engaging and difficult to solve.\n\n\n \nThe completed puzzle will be available in next week's Observer Digital Edition, offering a solution for those who find it challenging. This provides an opportunity for readers to check their work or understand how to solve the puzzle if they get stuck. The availability of the solution in a future edition also serves as an incentive to purchase the digital edition, supporting the publication while gaining access to exclusive content like the completed Sudoku puzzle.\n\n\n \nSolving the puzzle requires a combination of logical reasoning and attention to detail. Given the unique rules, each step must be carefully considered to ensure that the sum of the numbers in the grey-lined cells matches the corner figures and that no number is repeated within each shape. This process can be both frustrating and rewarding, as the solver navigates the challenges posed by the modified rules and the traditional Sudoku constraints.\n\n\n \nUltimately, the puzzle offers a fun and challenging way to exercise one's problem-solving skills. With its blend of traditional Sudoku rules and the added complexity of summing numbers within grey-lined cells, it provides an entertaining and intellectually stimulating activity. Whether one chooses to solve it on their own or refers to the solution in the Observer Digital Edition, the puzzle is sure to engage and challenge those who attempt it, making it a worthwhile pursuit for fans of Sudoku and puzzle enthusiasts alike.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.4018803536891937}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.04305700585246086}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0232519693672657}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.008725020103156567}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -7.486063259420916e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0031777145341038704}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011118361726403236}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.2270030528306961}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.002512990264222026}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.024781323969364166}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.008299149572849274}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0067192567512393}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -0.00012361239350866526}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.31154054403305054}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.0039595551788806915}, {"token": " rules", "logprob": -0.11019902676343918}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.02659463882446289}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.8281631469726562}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob": -0.047784850001335144}, {"token": " puzzle", "logprob": -0.0014821031363680959}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.0006300609675236046}, {"token": " explained", "logprob": -0.4565137028694153}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -5.864924969500862e-05}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -0.06154264509677887}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.